 "result_text": "I fixed the `notification.add` and `notification.update` errors, but I haven't run the tests or tried it against the real API.\n\nThe cause was in `rachiopy/rachioobject.py`. `_request` passed the payload dict straight to `requests` as `data=`, which form-encodes it instead of sending JSON. For nested payloads like `{\"device\": {\"id\": ...}}`, the server received `device=id` and failed with \"Unrecognized token 'device'\". `_request` now converts the body with `json.dumps` before sending, and sends nothing when there's no body.\n\nEvery other method that sends a payload goes through the same function, so the `device`, `zone` and `schedulerule` PUT calls now send JSON too. Their flat payloads were presumably accepted as form data before, so this should be harmless, but I haven't confirmed it.\n\nIf any existing tests assert on the exact `data=` argument, they will need updating, and I haven't checked for any.",
